{
  "title": "04 — Follow State Back to the Screen",
  "description": "The tool loop is only half the story. Now follow durable state in the other direction: discover the Brain, create and fork conversation branches, reconstruct a Transcript, and let the chat view paint that semantic record without taking ownership of it.",
  "nextTour": "05 — Learn How to Change Bolovan",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "src/brain-store.ts",
      "pattern": "async initialize\\(\\): Promise<void>",
      "title": "04.01 — The Brain wakes before the conversation",
      "description": "Initialization resolves the brain folder, ensures its structure, loads valid branch files, restores the selected branch when possible, and reports the resolved folder back to device-local settings. The Harness calls this once before any Run or session transition."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/brain-store.ts",
      "pattern": "private async resolveFolder\\(\\): Promise<string>",
      "title": "04.02 — A manifest makes the Brain discoverable",
      "description": "The configured folder wins when it contains `bolovan-brain.json`. Otherwise a single manifest elsewhere in the vault is auto-discovered; ambiguous or absent manifests fall back to configuration. This lets a synced Brain move without silently guessing between several candidates."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/brain-store.ts",
      "pattern": "private async ensureStructure\\(\\): Promise<void>",
      "title": "04.03 — Portable state is visible and ordinary",
      "description": "The store creates the Brain folder, `Skills/`, `Sessions/`, a manifest, and starter root `AGENTS.md` through Obsidian's Vault API. A legacy `Instructions.md` is renamed without changing its content. These deterministic plugin-owned paths need no model approval because their destinations and formats are fixed by product code."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/brain-store.ts",
      "pattern": "async instructions\\(\\): Promise<string>",
      "title": "04.04 — Instructions and skills disclose progressively",
      "description": "The store reads only complete root `AGENTS.md` as always-on policy. Adjacent Skill methods delegate strict discovery, metadata catalogs, activation, and bounded resources to the Skill module. The Harness reloads that state on every model round without flattening every procedure into the initial prompt."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/brain-store.ts",
      "pattern": "async newConversation\\(model: string\\): Promise<string>",
      "title": "04.05 — A new Conversation starts on this device",
      "description": "A fresh conversation and branch receive random ids, this device's id, timestamps, model, empty messages, and a temporary title. The branch path is selected and created immediately under `Sessions/`, making the empty session durable before its first prompt."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/brain-store.ts",
      "pattern": "async append\\(messages: ModelMessage\\[\\], model: string\\): Promise<void>",
      "title": "04.06 — Appending also maintains branch metadata",
      "description": "Append obtains a writable branch, extends its ordered messages, records the model and modification time, and replaces the temporary title with text derived from the first user message. One method keeps conversation content and its summary metadata coherent."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/brain-store.ts",
      "pattern": "private async writableBranch\\(",
      "title": "04.07 — A foreign Branch forks before writing",
      "description": "A branch owned by this device is returned directly. A foreign branch is copied into a new branch with a new branch id and this device's id, then selected before append. The remote history stays unchanged; sync conflicts are preserved as parallel histories instead of being guessed together."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/brain-store.ts",
      "pattern": "private async writeActive\\(",
      "title": "04.08 — Existing Branches write through `Vault.process`",
      "description": "New paths use `Vault.create`; existing conversation files use `Vault.process`. Filenames encode conversation, device, and branch ids under the visible `Sessions/` folder, allowing Obsidian Sync to transport each device-owned history as an ordinary file."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/brain-store.ts",
      "pattern": "private async reloadBranches\\(\\): Promise<void>",
      "title": "04.09 — Partial sync files remain on disk",
      "description": "Reload scans session JSON files, accepts only format-1 objects with message arrays, and ignores malformed or partial files without deleting them. A sync-conflicted artifact stays available for recovery even when it cannot become an active Branch."
    },
    {
      "file": "tests/brain-store.test.ts",
      "pattern": "describe\\(\"BrainStore device-owned branches\"",
      "title": "04.10 — Watch the fork invariant execute",
      "description": "The test opens a branch owned by a remote device, appends a local assistant message, and proves that the active path now belongs to the local device while the original remote branch still contains only its original history."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/transcript.ts",
      "pattern": "^export class Transcript",
      "title": "04.11 — Durable messages become semantic items",
      "description": "`Transcript` is the DOM-free record used by the chat surface. It owns append-only item order, assistant accumulation and finalization, tool pairing, history mapping, attachment display recovery, and synchronous change notifications. Painting remains somebody else's job."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/transcript.ts",
      "pattern": "^  loadHistory\\(messages: TranscriptHistoryMessage\\[\\]\\): void",
      "title": "04.12 — Switching sessions reconstructs the screen",
      "description": "`loadHistory` clears the current semantic items and replays persisted messages in order. User prompts recover visible text and attachment paths, assistant tool calls become running tool items, and later tool messages pair by call id and finalize them."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/transcript.ts",
      "pattern": "^  apply\\(event: BolovanEvent\\): void",
      "title": "04.13 — Live events use the same semantics",
      "description": "Text grows one open assistant item; a tool start finalizes that block and appends a running tool; a tool end completes the matching item; settlement closes the remaining assistant block; and an exited event becomes a visible system note. The rules do not depend on DOM timing."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/chat-view.ts",
      "pattern": "async onOpen\\(\\): Promise<void>",
      "title": "04.14 — The view attaches to long-lived state",
      "description": "Opening the chat builds its layout, subscribes to Transcript and Harness events, registers the approval responder, starts the Brain, loads the current Conversation, and tracks workspace changes for active-note context. Closing reverses subscriptions and cancels active work."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/chat-view.ts",
      "pattern": "private loadConversation\\(snapshot: BolovanConversationSnapshot\\)",
      "title": "04.15 — A snapshot replaces one rendered session",
      "description": "The view clears its element maps, rebuilds an empty transcript surface, asks `Transcript` to load persisted messages, repaints every resulting item, updates the session picker, and restores scroll and empty-state controls. Session switching is a coherent snapshot transition, not a stream of partial mutations."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/chat-view.ts",
      "pattern": "private onAgentEvent\\(event: BolovanEvent\\)",
      "title": "04.16 — Harness events cross one bridge",
      "description": "Conversation snapshots take the replacement path; text and tool events flow through `Transcript.apply`; settled and exited events close running UI state. After settlement, session summaries refresh because the completed Run may have created or forked a Branch."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/composer.ts",
      "pattern": "^export class Composer",
      "title": "04.17 — The composer keeps DOM editing local",
      "description": "The contenteditable composer renders labeled Note and Skill mentions, serializes them back to `[[wikilinks]]`, and drives one floating picker. It exposes plain text and send intent to the view; note attachment and explicit Skill activation policy remain in `context.ts`."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/chat-view.ts",
      "pattern": "private async openNote\\(file: TFile\\)",
      "title": "04.18 — Links leave the chat visible",
      "description": "When the user follows a transcript link or attachment, the note opens in the most recent non-chat leaf or a new tab. The chat leaf survives, matching the navigation invariant offered to the model through the `workspace` tool."
    },
    {
      "file": "tests/transcript.test.ts",
      "pattern": "describe\\(\"Transcript live events\"",
      "title": "04.19 — Prove the screen story without a screen",
      "description": "Transcript tests replay persisted exchanges and live event sequences to defend ordering, assistant finalization, tool pairing, targets, failures, notices, and continuity without an Obsidian DOM. Chapter 05 now shows how these tests, ADRs, and engineering rules govern future changes."
    }
  ]
}
